(*A session of its own rather than a theory inside Phi_Test, so that it can be built in seconds
  right after Phi_System and used as a fast gate.  Its subject is the syntax layer alone, so it
  deliberately depends on neither the semantics nor the standard library.*)
session "Phi_Syntax_Constraint_Test" = "Phi_System" +
  description "
    Regression tests for the positional constraints that Isabelle wraps around the head of a
    notated application.  When such a constraint stops a syntax translation from matching, the
    failure is silent -- a value list comes out short, a subjection collapses -- so an ordinary
    session can go on building green while the specifications it accepts have quietly changed
    meaning.  Nothing here can be left to the ordinary sessions to catch.
  "
  theories
    Phi_Syntax_Constraint_Test
